# Deployment Owner

The deployment owner username defaults to the **company display name** from admin → Company (override per install with `ADMIN_USERNAME`, comma-separated for multiple names).

Owner-only UI today:
- **Deploy wizard** (`/deploy`, `GET`/`POST /api/deploy/wizard`) — `deploy_wizard` module in `config/config-reave.json` only, plus official reΛVe.app host. Client installs 404. Dashboard tile is `footerNav: ["deploy"]` in that same file.
- **Industries** (account menu + `GET`/`PUT /api/admin/deck-industries`) — official reΛVe.app host only. Each industry is a deploy playbook (notes, modules, extras, sample data). Client installs hide the menu item and the API 404s. Deck/demo consumers still read the enabled list; the deploy wizard applies the playbook.
- **Catalog** (dashboard → Modules list + `GET`/`PUT /api/admin/module-catalog`) — official reΛVe.app host only. Sale-sheet flags, labels, prices, and groups for Core OS + add-ons. Client installs get deploy status only; the catalog API 404s. Public `/modules` and Add-ons read the overlay after load. `?tab=catalog` opens Modules.
- **Vapi sync** (`POST /api/admin/vapi`, `/vapi-sync` agent command)
- **Chat recovery** (`GET`/`POST /api/admin/chats`) — lists the distinct
  `user_id`s that own chat threads and reassigns threads orphaned under a
  previous Clerk user id (e.g. after a Clerk instance/key change) to the
  current owner. Postgres backend only.

Match is case-insensitive against the signed-in Clerk user's id (`AGENT_ALERT_USER_ID`), or `username`, `firstName`, `lastName`, full name, or primary email (full or local part).

Feature modules and admin navigation are configured per install in `config/config-{slug}.json` (not in the admin UI).
